    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d321">

                <pb facs="0719" n="685" xml:id="pg685"/>

                <head>321. Memorandum of a Telephone Conversation Between the President and the Secretary of State,
                    January 5, 1956, 9:48 a.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d321-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1956-01-05T09:48:00"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">January 5, 1956, 9:48
                        a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The Pres. said Kubitschek has gone—he is
                    very attractive—a nice guy—talks a little English. They talked about economic
                    development—he realized his dependence on us. The Pres. told K. he has
                    friendship here. Dunn can report more
                    fully. The Pres. told K. he can easily send a personal friend of his in the oil
                    business down and consult with him but the Pres.’s own observation would be any
                    plan for the slightest modification of their law should come from them &amp; not
                    seem to be inspired from here.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d321-f2"/> K. would like to
                    talk with someone in Feb. He might ask someone like Pete Jones.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d321-f3"/> K. said he is conservative and has come up in the spirit
                    of friendship and wants to help his country and act in a way that commands
                    respect.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d321-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d321-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Eisenhower Library, Dulles Papers, White House Telephone
                    Conversations. Prepared in the Office of the Secretary of State.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d321-f2" n="2" xml:id="d321-f2-content">
                <p>In a handwritten note, Dulles inserted the
                    phrase “&amp; not seem to be inspired from here” in the source text.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d321-f3" n="3" xml:id="d321-f3-content">
                <p>Dulles inserted this sentence in the
                    source text in a handwritten note. W. Alton (“Pete”) Jones was Chairman of the
                    Board and Director of Cities Services Oil Company.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
